hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18135","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Hisham who said: My father narrated to me that Ubaydullah ibn Adi narrated to him that two men informed him that they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking him for charity, so he looked them up and down and saw them sturdy, and said: If you wish, I will give you, but there is no share in it for a rich man nor for a strong earner."
"18136","Waki narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ubaydullah who said: Two men narrated to me that they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: So he looked up and down at them, and mentioned the hadith."
